  clock: 6  # fa6c
  nonce: fa6c  # fa6c
  message: "Cross-item review 2026-05-17: WI-totub filed as gating precondition (small clap::Parser experiment to determine whether 'rust-analyzer scip' default invocation surfaces proc-macro-expanded symbols at all). The proc-macro question was originally posed in WI-mirus-pupas (closed wont_do 2026-05-17, stale premise from before the silent-fall-through finding). Until WI-totub runs, the expected value of this item for wasm_bindgen.py / napi.py / tauri_ipc.py specifically is unknown — those three linkers' value depends entirely on whether SCIP carries the macro expansion. The other Rust-touching linkers in scope (jni.py for JNIEXPORT, cgo.py for cgo) are unaffected because their joins don't depend on proc-macros."  # fa6c
- op: discuss  # d4ab
  at: '2026-05-24T09:18:19Z'  # d4ab
  by: agent  # d4ab
  actor: jgstern_agent  # d4ab
  clock: 7  # d4ab
  nonce: d4ab  # d4ab
  message: "Scope assessment post-WI-totub (2026-05-24).\n\nWI-totub experiment result: default 'rust-analyzer scip <workspace>' does NOT surface proc-macro-expanded symbols. The clap::Parser-derived test crate produced SCIP output containing references INTO macro infrastructure (clap_builder Parser#parse, [Arg]long) but NOT the synthesized impl bodies (<Args as Parser>::parse, FromArgMatches, CommandFactory). Bonus check: the missing symbols are absent from raw index.scip itself, NOT dropped by the SCIP->IR translator. Full write-up at ~/hypergumbo_lab_notebook/notebookjournal_05242026_0516.md.\n\nPer-linker value distribution after WI-totub:\n\n| Linker | Original framing | Post-WI-totub value |\n|---|---|---|\n| tauri_ipc.py | 'biggest win' via #[tauri::command] | ~0 — macro-generated IPC wrapper not visible in SCIP |\n| wasm_bindgen.py | 'biggest win' via #[wasm_bindgen] | ~0 — exported wrapper not visible; JS-side join key still source-level fn name |\n| napi.py | 'biggest win' via N-API macros | ~0 — N-API wrapper not visible |\n| jni.py | confidence boost via mangling | Marginal — Rust JNI uses explicit #[no_mangle] extern \"C\" fn Java_*, matching key is source-level; SCIP adds confidence but not new edges |\n| cgo.py | listed in description | Zero — cgo links Go↔C, no Rust involvement (the description's listing here appears to be mis-stated) |\n\nThree of four real Rust-touching linkers gain ~0 from SCIP at the default invocation; one (jni.py) gains marginal confidence. The fifth (cgo.py) was mis-listed.\n\nRecommendation: stay todo_soft P4 someday with the WI-totub finding recorded. A future investigation into procMacro.enable=true could re-pilot — but that would be a NEW tracker item adjusting the 'rust-analyzer scip' invocation, not WI-burud's current scope (which gates on the DEFAULT invocation per the original description's gate question).\n\nDecision deferred to user. The honest deferral path mirrors WI-kofaf / WI-bimar's pattern earlier this session: substantial implementation cost (5 linkers, ~2461 LOC, both branches per linker + tests + bakeoff validation) with low expected value at the default SCIP invocation. Keeping todo_soft P4 someday until either (a) procMacro.enable=true is investigated and shown to surface the expanded symbols (would re-open the gate) or (b) the jni.py-only marginal-confidence-boost path is judged worth the linker-dispatch complexity (would require a re-scoping decision).\n\nCross-references:\n- WI-todon (PR #3895, closed 2026-05-24): diagnostic fix that made this experiment interpretable.\n- WI-totub (closed 2026-05-24): the gate question with the decisive answer.\n- WI-vovad (closed 2026-05-24): rust-analyzer validation curriculum.\n- WI-mirus-pupas (closed wont_do 2026-05-17): superseded predecessor.\n\nNo code change shipped against WI-burud this session."  # d4ab
